      "text": "The circuit never measures its qubits, so the simulator has no classical results to report and `get_counts` returns no meaningful GHZ distribution. I added an explicit measurement into the existing 3-bit classical register. I used `measure` rather than `measure_all()` because `measure_all()` would add a new register and change the count keys.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import Aer\nfrom qiskit import execute\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit\n\ncirc = QuantumCircuit(3, 3)\ncirc.h(0)\ncirc.cx(0, 1)\ncirc.cx(0, 2)\n# FIX: circuit had no measurement operations -> added measure of qubits 0,1,2 into classical bits 0,1,2, because counts only exist for measured classical bits\ncirc.measure([0, 1, 2], [0, 1, 2])\n\nbackend = Aer.get_backend(\"qasm_simulator\")\njob = execute(circ, backend, shots=100000)\nresult = job.result()\ncounts = result.get_counts(circ)\nprint(counts)\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
